    "A": "Develop the primary sequential candidate: stream input into an O(N^2) two-stage rolling sum. Let W=N-S+1; retain only S rows of W horizontal S-cell sums, update W vertical sums per row, and take the maximum after row S-1. Use signed 64-bit accumulators/ring values, initialize maxima from the first valid window, and handle negative values. This cuts memory versus the source’s matrix and avoids its O(S(N-S+1)^2) traversal. Validate S=1, S=N-1, and signed/extreme inputs; do not rely on fixed cases.",
